.\" Csh Shell — Man Page
.TH Context 1 "2026-07-17" "context 0.70.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
context \- a fast, fully configurable POSIX shell written in Rust
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B context
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B context
.B \-c
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B context
is a POSIX shell written entirely in Rust, featuring a custom line editor
with syntax highlighting, true-color theming via TOML configuration,
persistent command history, job control, and 30+ built-in commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c \fIcommand\
Execute the given command and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Syntax highlighting
Real-time highlighting of variables ($VAR), operators (|, &&, ;),
quoted strings, and command names in the input line.
.TP
.B True color
Any hex color (#RRGGBB) works via 24-bit ANSI escape sequences.
.TP
.B TOML configuration
Full configuration at ~/.config/context/c.toml with 15 sections.
.TP
.B Job control
Background jobs (cmd &), jobs/fg/bg builtins.
.TP
.B Command substitution
$(cmd) and backtick `cmd` forms.
.TP
.B Here documents and here strings
<<EOF and <<<string redirections.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Interrupt current process / cancel input line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Exit shell (when input is empty).
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Clear screen and redraw prompt.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Reverse incremental search through history.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Move cursor to beginning of line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Move cursor to end of line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Kill from cursor to end of line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+U
Kill from cursor to beginning of line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Delete word before cursor.
.TP
.B Tab
Command completion (PATH + current directory).
.TP
.B Up/Down
Navigate command history.
.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
cd, exit, export, unset, alias, unalias, source, history, set, env,
pwd, type, which, echo, printf, test, let, pushd, popd, dirs, readonly,
declare, jobs, fg, bg, exec, true, false, builtin.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration file: \fI~/.config/context/c.toml\
.br
Startup file: \fI~/.ctxrc\
.br
History file: \fI~/.ctx/.history\
.SH CURSOR FORMAT
The cursor is fully customizable via ~/.config/context/c.toml\.
.PP
Single character:
.PP
.RS 4
[cursor]
.br
symbol = "_"
.RE
.PP
Multi-line format (overrides symbol):
.PP
.RS 4
[cursor]
.br
format = ["├── ", "│   ", "└── "]
.br
format_align = "left"
.br
format_colorize = true
.RE
.PP
Each string in \fBformat\ is one line. The last line receives input.
Any character or Unicode symbol works.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/context/c.toml
Main configuration file (15 sections: history, cursor, prompt, box_config,
colors, symbols, ascii, execution, startup, editor, display, completion,
signals, environment, branding).
.TP
.I ~/.ctxrc
Sourced on startup for aliases, exports, and environment.
.TP
.I ~/.ctx/.history
Persistent command history.
